
  [1mThe main design choice: build the page from the vendored Keel kit.[0m The repo already has components for nearly
  everything the spec asks for: [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m with [38;5;153mselectField[39m (which reloads the page on change through
  [38;5;153mkit.js[39m), [38;5;153mdataTable[39m (sorting, ▲/▼ arrows, [38;5;153maria-sort[39m), [38;5;153mbadge[39m (with green, red, amber and blue tones) and [38;5;153memptyState[39m. The
  Services page builds its own table, select and pills, so I copied its [3mbehavior[0m rather than its markup:
  - unknown query values fall back to the defaults
  - sort links keep [38;5;153menv[39m
  - the filter form keeps [38;5;153msort[39m and [38;5;153mdir[39m in hidden inputs

  The kit's CSS already styles every class the page uses, so there are no stylesheet changes.

